've been  privileged to have you know the to keep  people who are the greatest in my  opinion in the history of the ninety  nine year history of the NFL at their  positions and keeping them together  it'll be two decades next year and  that's that's the main task of ownership  it is its historic and it's  unprecedented and I know Tom has said in  an interview that there's zero chance  that this is his last NFL season and so  his coach Belichick definitely coming  back to we we have a great pact he loves  what he does he's so good at it we've  created an environment where he can work  to the best of his abilities so I'm  quite confident he'll be back when you  think about their team and they walk out  on that field on Sunday or run out on  the field on Sunday what's the message  that you want to have in their mind you  you might never be there again it took  us over 30 years to get to our first  game so we we try to make sure that  people are completely focused on nothing  else but the game and doing what they  can to close the order we we've had a  pretty good record the last few years  and on Sunday we had a little throwing a  going-away party for our fans and 35,000  people came out on a Sunday really just  for seeing the players and coaches for  20 minutes so fans have been a big part  of our success and the support they've  given us well we are looking forward to  the game on Sunday congratulations on 25  years of ownership we but wish both the  Patriots and the Rams a good safe fun  game we will all be watching mr. Kraft  thank you so much thanks and just know  that the last thing coach is going to  tell the team we need CBS to get good  ratings  you do what you got to do to make that  out the Patriots and the Rams and all  those great players there's no doubt it  will be huge ratings thank you so much  and you guys snore thank you and you can  catch Super Bowl 53 and all the pregame  festivities right here on CBS starting  at 6:00 p.m. Eastern this Sunday when